# Generate 3D with the free Hugging Face Spaces: a job that comes back without a model, or a Space that has switched
# Text to 3D off, says so in red under Generate (service name included) instead of looking silent. After the refusal
# the Generate button stays greyed for that model (this session only: nothing is probed) until "Try again".
# A stub answers with the Spaces' real wording (generator_stub textoff / nomodel; never the network).
# Each wait is for the job itself (wait_idle, then the Try again button that only the refusal shows): the stub runs on a
# worker thread, so on a slow Windows runner the answer lands later than a fixed wait or "no candidates yet".
# CMake runs it at 1440x900 and 2880x1800 (the review sizes).
run ui_look look=classic layout=classic
run new_sphere subdivisions=3
drop ../../assets/demo/teddy-sketch.png
wait_for "Generate 3D/Generate 3D model" 5

generator_stub nomodel
click "Generate 3D/Generate 3D model"
click "Allow##send"
click OK
wait 0.3
wait_idle 60
expect_text finished without a model: try again or another provider
shot generate-no-model

click "Generate 3D/From text"
type "##textprompt" a stylised dragon head
generator_stub textoff
click "Generate 3D/Generate 3D model"
wait 0.3
wait_idle 60
wait_for "Generate 3D/Try again" 30
expect_text Text to 3D failed
expect_text Hunyuan3D 2 mini Turbo
expect_text switched Text to 3D off
expect_text Try again
shot generate-text-off

click "Generate 3D/Try again"
expect_no_text switched Text to 3D off
expect "Generate 3D/Generate 3D model"
expect_value http_requests == 0
generator_stub off
